From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt DeVillier <matt.devillier@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:19:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg: Add option to enable Secure Boot default
 after key enrollment

[ouroBIOS: commit 77242a1903be of MrChromebox's edk2, without the files
that TianoCore's tree does not have (tools/edk2-import.py): 3 in
edk2/OuroBiosPkg]

Add SECURE_BOOT_DEFAULT_ENABLE / PcdSecureBootDefaultEnable so
EnrollDefaultKeys can leave SecureBoot enabled after provisioning
default keys, instead of always forcing it off.

Use '-D SECURE_BOOT_DEFUALT_ENABLE=TRUE' to enable by default.

Signed-off-by: Matt DeVillier <matt.devillier@gmail.com>
---
 UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec b/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec
index 48d77955f6a0ce6224d358abf3478fb20284fa26..3e5bc43d99e5bca8c60b2bc0e2a4a727efed3d03 100644
--- a/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec
+++ b/UefiPayloadPkg/UefiPayloadPkg.dec
@@ -153,3 +153,8 @@ gUefiPayloadPkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdUseUniversalPayloadSerialPort|TRUE|BOOLEAN|0x00
 
 ## Indicates whether allows PCI Root Bridge to allocate DMA memory resource above 4G
 gUefiPayloadPkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdPciAllocateMemoryAbove4GB|FALSE|BOOLEAN|0x0000002E
+
+## If TRUE, EnrollDefaultKeys leaves Secure Boot enabled after provisioning
+#  default PK/KEK/db/dbx. If FALSE (legacy MrChromebox behavior), keys are
+#  enrolled but SecureBootEnable/SecureBoot remain disabled until toggled in setup.
+gUefiPayloadPkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdSecureBootDefaultEnable|FALSE|BOOLEAN|0x0000002F
